# Customer Email Salutation (Mr / Ms)

Order receipt, deal sheet, RFQ confirmation, KYC emails, and similar customer communications must greet using **Mr.** or **Ms.** from the customer profile — never guess or default incorrectly.

## Canonical helpers (`@root/schema`)

```typescript
import {
  getEmailSalutationFromSources,
  getOptionalEmailTitleFromSources,
  getEmailSalutationFromGender,
  resolveGenderForEmailSalutation,
} from "@root/schema";
```

| Gender | Salutation |
|--------|------------|
| `MALE` / `M` | **Mr.** |
| `FEMALE` / `F` | **Ms.** |
| Missing / `OTHER` / `NA` | **Mr. / Ms.** (fallback only) |

**Resolve gender** in this order: profile `gender` → `panCard.gender` → `aadhaarCard.gender` (KYC often stores gender only on documents).

```typescript
// Plain-text / PDF "Dear …" (includes Mr. / Ms. fallback)
const salutation = getEmailSalutationFromSources(profile);

// HTML templates with optional title?: "Mr." | "Ms."
const title = getOptionalEmailTitleFromSources(profile);
```

## Corporate customers

When `userType === "CORPORATE"`, use **`Dear Sir / Madam,`** instead of Mr/Ms + personal name (see deal sheet email flow).

## Where this applies

- Order receipt & deal sheet PDF emails (`send_deal_sheet_nyOrderId.ts`, `order_settlement.service.ts`)
- CRM email PDF flows (`orders.controller`, `GeneratePdfContent.tsx`)
- Place-order / RFQ confirmation (`place-order-email.ts`, proposals)
- KYC & account emails (`customer.manage_accounts`, `kyc_store`, `webhook_notification`, auth signup reminder)
- Order PDF salutation line (`packages/kyc-providers/pdf/helper.ts`)

## Do not

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — defaults non-MALE to Ms (wrong for unknown gender)
const salutation = customer.gender === "MALE" ? "Mr." : "Ms.";

// ❌ BAD — inline duplicate logic; misses PAN/Aadhaar fallback
const salutation = gender === "FEMALE" ? "Ms." : gender === "MALE" ? "Mr." : "Mr. / Ms.";

// ❌ BAD — PDF helper defaulting unknown gender to Mr
const salutation = genderRaw === "FEMALE" ? "Ms." : "Mr.";
```

Always use the shared helpers; extend `email_salutation.ts` if resolution rules change — do not copy logic into each email template.
